  "text": "2.2 Hello everybody! Thanks for helping me with my work. That's okay. Thanks for sending those photos, Keiko. No problem, Munira. Okay. I want to write about how people feel about the seasons. Is it good to live in a place where the weather is always the same? Or better to have four different seasons? Keiko, you're in Singapore. Yeah. I'm near the equator. The temperature is the same all year, around 30 degrees Celsius. There isn't winter, spring, or autumn. It's like summer every day. But between November and February, it's very wet. It's the rainy season. I don't like it. It's very different from the weather in Japan. Do you like the weather in Japan, Keiko? Okay. So, I'm from Japan. There are four seasons, and I like that. I like wearing different clothes at different times of the year. I'm from Tokyo, and the weather in Tokyo gets cold in winter. I love putting on a coat and going outside at that time of year. My favorite season is spring. In Japan, you can see pink flowers on the trees, and people have parties under them. I don't like doing things in hot weather. What about where you live, Lin? You're in Scotland. Yeah, I am. Keiko, is it 30 degrees where you are now? Yes. Wow. It's only 13 degrees here. It feels cold, but it's summer. The temperature doesn't change much here. It's usually between 5 and 15 degrees. But there are four seasons here in Scotland. For me, autumn is best. I love the red and orange colors of the trees in the autumn. I don't like winter in my country. Winter is long, and the nights are dark. It's dark early. Right now, it gets dark late. I love that. What about you, Munira? Well, there are four seasons in my country, Saudi. I don't like the summer because it's always very hot. Winters are short. The temperature in my city is around 9 degrees. There's snow in my country, but not much. But I love snow. There's a shopping center here with snow inside it every day. What? A shopping center? Yes, I go there a lot. I can send you a photo.",
